      "properties": {
        "name": "Warden Mella",
        "look": "0",
        "facing": "1",
        "says": "Ashholt keeps its gate shut after dark. The road south is safe enough by day - past the bridge, less so.|You'll want a bed at the inn before you try the pass. Nobody crosses the Vale tired and lives to say it was easy."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "npc",
      "column": 14,
      "row": 9,
      "properties": {
        "name": "Old Ferran",
        "look": "1",
        "facing": "1",
        "says": "Sixty years I've swept this square. The mountains east were quiet for fifty-nine of them.|Ash falls on the eastern ridge now. Not from any fire I can find. Somebody ought to walk up there and look."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "npc",
      "column": 11,
      "row": 13,
      "properties": {
        "name": "Bea",
        "look": "2",
        "facing": "0",
        "says": "The store's up the north road, past the well. Say I sent you and it'll cost you exactly the same.|My brother went east with a lantern and good boots. That was eleven days ago. I'd count that a long errand."
      }
    }
